{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "exMrY_6xoTahcTnBt",
			"description": "Autopistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cheap, mass-produced sidearm found across a billion hive worlds: gang muscle, PDF conscripts and Guard officers who don't rate a laspistol all carry one. Consistently portrayed in Guard and Arbites fiction as the low-status \"poor man's laspistol.\"\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers stub weapons directly, but they must stay consistent with the autogun anchor (5d+1 pi) they're built alongside. GURPS's own real-world pistol-calibre baseline (a modern 9mm Parabellum ball round, roughly 2d+2 pi) already sits at almost exactly the same fraction of the new autogun that the old 2d pi- sat below the old autogun (avg 9 / avg 18.5 = 49%, versus the old 7 / 15 = 47%), so the autopistol is set to that real 9mm figure rather than derived by pure arithmetic scaling: full pi wounding (not pi-) reflects a modern jacketed round rather than the crude ball ammo the earlier pass assumed. Against flak (DR 12) it penetrates just 8.3% of hits — a real but unimpressive threat, matching the autopistol's reputation as a backup weapon rather than a main-line arm. The Manstopper usage keeps the same pi+/divisor(0.5) shape as before, bumped by the same +2 average as the ball round (2d+3, avg 10): it never penetrates flak or better (0% of hits, effective DR doubled by the divisor) but hits unarmoured flesh harder, the standard GURPS way to model an expanding round — more damage to flesh, worse against any DR.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
