		{
			"id": "eMqUJlv_ICTqngWle",
			"description": "Autogun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard-issue solid-slug battle rifle of regiments and militias that lack a lasgun allocation — a recoil-operated intermediate-calibre rifle that recurs across Astra Militarum background material as the \"poor cousin\" of the lasgun, more common on low-priority garrison and PDF postings.\n\nDesign: Fixed autogun anchor (5d+1 pi): calibrated to lasgun parity rather than to flak. In the fiction autoguns kill as readily as lasguns, and Only War gives both the same damage, so the autogun is set for the same practical lethality as the lasgun anchor (5d(2) burn, avg 17.5) without copying its armour divisor — a solid slug has no focusing trick to help it through DR. Average roll 18.5 gets through flak (DR 12) on 94.1% of hits and mesh (DR 15) on 77.9%, both comparable to the lasgun's own flak/mesh numbers; against carapace (DR 45) it penetrates 0% of hits, even worse than the lasgun's rare 9.8% since it has no armour divisor to help it — confirming \"stopped by carapace.\" An earlier draft used 2d+2 pi to make flak \"stop stub rounds\"; that framework wording was about pistol calibres and has been corrected. Range 500/2000 fits an intermediate-calibre rifle. RoF 10, 30(3) follow selective-fire rifle conventions. The Dum-Dum usage applies the same expanding-round logic as the autopistol's Manstopper, bumped the same +1 die as the ball round.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "8 lb",
