		{
			"id": "eGE58NvXGebFKBY9S",
			"description": "Stub Revolver",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A well-made, reliable break-top or swing-cylinder handgun favoured by Inquisitorial acolytes, enforcers and anyone who prizes reliability over firepower or rate of fire; FFG-line background (used here only for relative calibration, per framework.md's source order) singles the stub revolver out as the higher-quality, slower-firing counterpart to the stub automatic.\n\nDesign: Single-action cycling caps RoF at 1 — there's no autofire mechanism. A heavier, hand-loaded magnum-class round (GURPS real-world baseline: a .44 Magnum runs about 3d pi) sits above the autopistol's 9mm-class 2d+2 pi, reflecting a larger-calibre, better-machined round fired from a tighter, hand-fitted barrel — and stays well under the autogun's 5d+1 pi rifle round, the same gap the old 2d+1 kept below the old 4d+1 autogun. Average roll 10.5 penetrates flak (DR 12) on 25.9% of hits (better than the autopistol's 8.3%), mesh (DR 15) on 4.6%, and never beats carapace (DR 45: 0%). Low Rcl (1) follows from GURPS convention for a heavier, well-balanced revolver.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "140",
