		{
			"id": "egbMrzIvOXBAZnZmZ",
			"description": "Heavy Stubber",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's standard heavy machine gun: a deliberately archaic solid-slug design valued precisely because a forge world with almost no infrastructure can still manufacture it. A mainstay on Chimera pintles, Sentinel weapon mounts and heavy-weapon squads across Guard background art and fiction, and never once shown killing a tank.\n\nDesign: Scaled up from the autogun's pi rating to a true heavy-calibre weapon (pi+, the GURPS x1.5 wounding multiplier), landing close to GURPS's own real-world .50-calibre benchmark (roughly 6d+2 pi+) rather than any 40k catalogue entry. Deliberately pitched well below the heavy bolter anchor (7d×2(2) pi++, which \"chews light vehicles\" at AV10): 6d+2 pi+ averages 23 with no armour divisor, penetrating 0% of hits against AV10 (DR 100). That failure is intentional and total — the fiction never shows a heavy stubber meaningfully hurting a vehicle, only infantry, and this stat block reproduces that gap explicitly and by a wider margin than the old DR 50 threshold did. Mounted per framework.md's braced/mounted-heavies rule, hence Gunner (Machine Gun) rather than Guns.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "900",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WneBpbcLVayw2eqe4",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "pi+",
						"base": "6d+2"
					},
					"accuracy": "4",
					"range": "500/2000",
					"rate_of_fire": "10",
					"shots": "250(20)",
					"bulk": "-6",
					"recoil": "3",
					"strength": "12B",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Gunner"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Machine Gun"
							}
