		{
			"id": "eCBBOcoit4P8Su45p",
			"description": "Hunting Rifle",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A bolt-action precision rifle common on agri, feral and frontier worlds, pressed into service as a stopgap sniper weapon by Guard marksmen and PDF units where a long-las isn't issued.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a realistic TL7 bolt-action big-game rifle (a real-world analogue, not a renamed catalogue item), scaled up in the same proportion as the other stub-tech weapons in this file: a large single round for maximum penetration (average 24.5), RoF 1 for manual bolt cycling between shots. Kept below the long-las (6d(2) burn) in practical terms — full pi wounding and no armour divisor mean it's comparably lethal to an unarmoured target (99.7% through flak, DR 12) but does nothing against carapace-or-better armour (0% of hits at DR 45), in contrast to the long-las which at least keeps pace with a standard lasgun there.",
